renderer: the museum's wallhack, for recordings only

r_demo_xray: after the normal draw, a player is drawn again with the depth
test reversed, no texture and one bright colour, so the part of them behind
a wall shows as a bright shape — the OpenGL wrapper wallhacks of 2000-2004
made visible, the "chams" of the years after. Nothing outside a recording,
whatever the cvar says; and only the players the server sent, which was the
anti-wallhack of its day. It sits in R_StudioDrawPoints because that is
where every path draws: the Counter-Strike client has a studio renderer of
its own and calls back into the engine only to emit the triangles, so a
switch in the engine's own player routine (the first try) was never reached.

